  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, written in the same style as the earlier entries. The version and date come from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files.\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads with backoff when the server returns 503 (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nACME-421 (removing the deprecated `--legacy` flag from sync) is left out as you asked. It was the only change marked as breaking (the `!` in `ACME-421!`). With it gone, this release has no breaking changes, so the `--legacy` flag is still available. That makes a minor version bump to 2.4.0 the right size.\n\nI left out author credits (@mira, @jonas, etc.) because earlier entries don't include them. I can add them if you want.",
